steps.message:
The remaining docs describe the exact developer UX (“Psst, here’s your code”) and confirm the pending token is likely stateless. A good reconstruction is:

1. generate a random six-character code;
2. put a bcrypt digest plus identity reference into an encrypted, 15-minute pending token;
3. set that token as an HttpOnly cookie (and return it for JSON);
4. email/log the raw code;
5. verify `code` at `/session/magic_link`, consume the pending cookie, and create the normal session.

This avoids a migration, naturally expires at 15 minutes, and matches the documented API. I’ll verify Rails encrypted-cookie handling and inspect development docs/UI styling before implementing this core sign-in path, then layer sign-up and join intent onto it.

